Notes close at their own bracket: a^[a \] b] and the text goes on.

A link around math: [range $[0,1)$](u) is one link.

#strong[code `a]b` here] and the body ends after the code span.

Code spans by run length: ``a`b``, `` `tick` `` and ` x `; an unclosed `` run stays literal.

Pairs skip stray brackets: *range [0, 1) only* and _see [sic_ ok.

Math decodes only the dollar escape: $a \$ b$ and $x \, y$.

Islands that would swallow a closer: [price $5](u) and #strong[cost $3] then $x$ after.

= Targets <tgt>

== An odd label <a]b>

References: @[ tgt ] and @[a\]b] in brackets.
